{
  "_comment": "Rooms, corridors and adjacency traced from assets/ship/hull_plate.png. The simulation reads `adjacent` and `capacity` only \u2014 polygons, doors and the corridor graph are for the viewer. Ids must not change: scene scripts and save data key off them.",
  "_plate": "Compartments are drawn by the plate. Nothing in ui/ draws hull, floors or bulkheads. Every coordinate here is in plate pixels, so all of it is independent of window size.",
  "_layout": "Thirteen compartments, traced off the bulkhead bands in the art. Twelve are the rooms the owner specified; the thirteenth is the magazine, which is a fully walled compartment on the plate sitting beside turret control, so leaving it out would have left a visible room crew could never enter.",
  "_corridors": "The plate paints a yellow guidance stripe down the centre of every corridor. `waypoints` are traced off that stripe at each junction, bend and doorway; `corridor_edges` join them; `room_doors` tap each compartment onto the graph. ui/ walks this polyline so crew stop cutting through bulkheads. Corridors that dead-end against the hull carry no waypoints \u2014 they are cosmetic.",
  "_adjacency": "Derived from the corridor, not hand-listed: two rooms are adjacent when their doorways are consecutive taps on the graph. The simulation charges one transit per hop, so this is what movement costs.",
  "plate": "res://assets/ship/hull_plate.png",
  "plate_normal": "res://assets/ship/hull_plate_normal.png",
  "plate_size": [
    1797,
    875
  ],
